Models
- Inkling 2 Mini (https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini), by Thinking Machines Lab,
  Apache-2.0.
- Inkling-2-Mini-oQ2.5e-mtp (https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/Inkling-2-Mini-oQ2.5e-mtp), MLX weights
  by the mlx-community, Apache-2.0, revision d4a4f3f (the drafter file is not downloaded).

Runtime
- oMLX (https://github.com/jundot/omlx), Apache-2.0, installed from its Homebrew tap (tested with 0.8.2).
  Nuemac runs on oMLX's Python stack and uses its Inkling 2 model code, chat handling and Inkling output
  parser; engine/families/inkling2 replaces the model's KV caches, the global layers' decode attention and
  the loop-controller mixing, and requantizes the output head at load.
- MLX and mlx-lm (https://github.com/ml-explore), MIT, Copyright Apple Inc., as shipped with oMLX.

Comparison builds (benchmarked in the docs, not installed by Nuemac)
- llama.cpp / ggml (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), MIT, release b12600, with
  Inkling-2-Mini-AD-IQ3_XXS.gguf from AtomicChat/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF (Apache-2.0).
- PrismML llama.cpp fork (https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp), MIT, with Ternary Bonsai 2 27B by
  PrismML (Apache-2.0), derived from Qwen3.8-27B by the Qwen team (Alibaba Cloud).

Ideas and method
- TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold), MIT: the engine + supported-models + recipes layout.
- Strata (https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata), MIT: kernel and dispatch ideas evaluated in the recipe.
- inference-optimisation-skill (https://github.com/sybil-solutions/inference-optimisation-skill), MIT, by
  Sybil Solutions: the ceilings-first, one-change-per-experiment tuning method behind docs/recipes.
